        <briefdescription>
<para>Expands file and directory paths into sorted entries. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each path is resolved one time here, so that a verb reads the file it receives and resolves nothing again.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rawPaths</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="class_input" kindref="compound">Input</ref> file or directory paths. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>includeGlobs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Wildcard patterns (<computeroutput>*</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>?</computeroutput>) a file name or path must match when non-empty. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>excludeGlobs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Wildcard patterns that exclude matching files. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>isIncludingHidden</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>True to include dot-prefixed entries. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>isIgnoringRules</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>True to bypass <computeroutput>.gitignore</computeroutput> and global exclude rules.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Pair of: the failures, each with its failure result, in the order found: first the failures of the raw paths, in the order given, then the failures of the folder walk, by worker index; and the entries, one per file, sorted by display path, each with its display path, its resolved file, and its explicit flag, true when the file was named on the command line.</para>
</simplesect>
A file named on the command line wins over the same file found by the walk. The sort puts the explicit entry first among entries with the same display path, and the duplicate removal keeps the first entry. The duplicate removal runs only when more than one raw path is given. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
