        <briefdescription>
<para>Walks each root and reports each included file. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns each unreadable folder.</para>
<para>Each root is one item of one walk, so that many small roots do not each start and join threads. A folder item reads its listing once and publishes that listing. The folder item then walks the first 64 entries of the listing. Each further range of 64 entries of the same listing is one more item. Symbolic links and Windows junctions are neither walked nor reported. A folder that cannot be read, or whose listing fails part-way, is unreadable. It is returned, not reported through onFile. The walk runs on worker threads. Each callback receives the index of its worker. One thread uses one worker index at a time, so a caller keeps one slot per worker and needs no lock. The order of the callbacks is not defined.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>roots</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pairs of the caller-supplied root path prefix, used in display paths, and the resolved directory to walk. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>includeGlobs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Wildcard patterns (<computeroutput>*</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>?</computeroutput>) a file must match when non-empty. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>excludeGlobs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Wildcard patterns that exclude matching files. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>isIncludingHidden</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>True to include dot-prefixed entries. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>isIgnoringRules</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>True to bypass <computeroutput>.gitignore</computeroutput> and global exclude rules. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>onWorkerCount</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callback invoked once before the walk, with the number of workers. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>onFile</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callback invoked per matching file with <computeroutput>(workerIndex, fullPath, displayPath)</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>shouldStop</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Atomic cancellation flag polled during the walk.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The unreadable folders, each with its display path and its read failure. The order depends on the walk, so it is not defined. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
